<title>USA: Macerich Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>Macerich Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA MONICA, Calif 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Unaudited)</p>
<p>			 (In Thousands, Except Per Share Amounts)</p>
<p>				    Results Of Operations</p>
<p>			    (For The Quarter Ended March 31,)</p>
<p>						1997			   1996</p>
<p>    Minimum rents			32,053			22,638</p>
<p>    Percentage rents		    2,206			 1,570</p>
<p>    Tenant recoveries		  14,917			10,524</p>
<p>    Other revenue			 1,126			   560</p>
<p>    Total Revenues		     50,302			35,292</p>
<p>    Shopping Center expenses	 15,761			11,028</p>
<p>    Depreciation and amortization   9,474			 7,751</p>
<p>General, administrative</p>
<p>     and other expenses		   750			   789</p>
<p>    Interest expense		   14,766			 9,841</p>
<p>Equity in net</p>
<p>income of joint ventures</p>
<p>     and the management companies     368			 1,181</p>
<p>Income prior to</p>
<p>allocation of</p>
<p>     minority interest		  9,919			 7,064</p>
<p>Income allocated</p>
<p>     to minority interests	    3,168			 2,664</p>
<p>    Net income			    6,751			 4,400</p>
<p>    Number of shares outstanding   25,799			19,978</p>
<p>Average number</p>
<p>     of OP Units outstanding	 37,904			32,073</p>
<p>    Net income per share		$0.26			 $0.22</p>
<p>Dividend declared</p>
<p>     and paid per share		 $0.44			 $0.42</p>
<p>    Funds from operations (a)	19,471			14,564</p>
<p>    Funds from operations per share$0.514			$0.454</p>
<p>(a) Funds from operations is defined as net income (computed in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles), excluding gains (or losses) from debt restructuring and sales of property, plus depreciation and amortization (excluding; depreciation of personal property, amortization of financing costs and amortization of financial instruments), and after adjustments for unconsolidated partnerships and joint ventures.  Adjustments for unconsolidated joint ventures and partnerships will be calculated on the same basis.  FFO does not represent cash flow from operations, as defined by generally accepted accounting principles and is not necessarily indicative of cash available to fund all cash flow needs.</p>
